{
  "about": "Game terms that are drawn with their icon in front of them wherever they appear in card text. Icons are the Varak ve mine set in art/icons/set (<icon>.png master, <icon>-144/-72/-48.png); inline text uses -48. Ids follow the manual (term.*, card.*). Character names use the short forms from the manual (Süleyman is term.suleyman). Entries with \"display\": \"icon\" are drawn as the icon alone, with the words as a tooltip (title and aria-label), not inline text: the three use frequencies.",
  "match": {
    "rule": "A stem matches at the start of a word and runs on through any following letters, so Turkish suffixes stay attached (Nüfuzu, Vekile, Divan'da). Matching is case-sensitive: list a lowercase stem only where the term is written in lowercase in running text. Try longer stems first, so Saray Dedikodusu wins over Saray and Birinci Vekil over Vekil.",
    "regex": "(?<![\\p{L}\\p{N}])(STEMS)(?:['’]\\p{L}+|\\p{L}*)",
    "flags": "gu",
    "note": "Use \\p{L} with the u flag, not \\b: \\b treats ı, ş and ğ as word breaks. A short stem also matches longer unrelated words that start with it (Kul in Kullan), so avoid starting a sentence with such a word in card text. Elements marked data-noterms (frequency pills) and power names (class pn) are skipped, so a name like Kulis never picks up the Kul icon."
  },
